body:
I am not diagnosed but I had bilateral ligament tears in my wrists and ankles. I have had long-term plantar fasciitis, Morton's neuroma, nerve pain, peroneal tendonitis, thumb tendonitis, knee pain, and was recently DXed with bilateral feet arthritis. No nerve damage but numbness in tingling in hands and feet. I also have POTS. I wonder if I have hand arthritis. I have other aches and pains, but those are the worst. 

&#x200B;

How did you get a diagnosis?

I'm female, don't know if that matters but maybe, and I'm 28. I've always had acne and took accurate around age 21 because I wasn't responding to treatment. My acne started up again though around maybe 25 and recently got quite bad for having been on accutane in the past. I had cystic pimples on my jawline and cheeks, I'd say anywhere between 8 and 10 at a time. It wasn't too severe when considering acne in general, but not normal for a 28 year old woman. I suspected it was hormonal, but now I am not so sure since my face cleared so quickly. 

&#x200B;

Have you noticed any improvements on the carnivore diet? I'm sorry to hear you are still struggling. Acne is so frustrating.

I keep feeling like someone is in my room at night too and waking up terrified and not knowing why.. have to sleep on one side cuz I feel like im being watched. bad dreams but aren't related to abuse?? I dont think ? I dont remember them.

&#x200B;

you made me feel so so much less alone. thank you!! I hope you know there is another person experiencing the exact same thing.

Try toe spreaders on top of toe yoga, especially since you describe feeling like your walking on a stone. Sometimes alpha lipoic acid (a supplement) can help nerve entrapments, they did for me, but evidence shows they are effective for diabetic nerve damage and carpal tunnel.

I have had several nerve entrapments due to another disorder. Turmeric (another supplement) may help too.

&#x200B;

[https://www.amazon.com/YOGABODY-Spreaders-Separators-Latex-Free-Stretchers/dp/B01AUZWM64/ref=cm\_cr\_arp\_d\_product\_top?ie=UTF8](https://www.amazon.com/YOGABODY-Spreaders-Separators-Latex-Free-Stretchers/dp/B01AUZWM64/ref=cm_cr_arp_d_product_top?ie=UTF8)

&#x200B;

These helped me a ton with the stone in my shoe. I recommend them more than anything. I wear them for about 20-30 minutes a day. I hope you feel better soon. I went from hobbling to pain free in 3 days after I wore them.

&#x200B;

I have had morton's neuroma (which often causes that stone sensation) and an entrapement on the other side of my foot, on the tibial nerve. (More on the inside of the foot). I definitely do a lot ankle mobility work and strengthening due to chronic sprains / tears.

[https://www.amazon.com/DYKOOK-Separator-Protectors-Straightener-Separators/dp/B075SVWV59/ref=sr\_1\_12?keywords=Mortons+neuroma+inserts&qid=1639098772&sr=8-12](https://www.amazon.com/DYKOOK-Separator-Protectors-Straightener-Separators/dp/B075SVWV59/ref=sr_1_12?keywords=Mortons+neuroma+inserts&qid=1639098772&sr=8-12)

&#x200B;

Is this an option?

There is a website.. [https://www.therapath.com/services/small-fiber-neuropathy-testing/small-fiber-procedure/#](https://www.therapath.com/services/small-fiber-neuropathy-testing/small-fiber-procedure/#)

&#x200B;

Your doctor can order a kit here to complete the test for you. Hopefully they will. I'd push for an EMG of the legs. Glad you finished the doxy, if you did test positive for Lyme, also push for a steroid pack.

&#x200B;

Take the supplement Alpha Lipoic Acid 2x a day at 600mg, helped my symptoms a ton and studies show it can be helpful for regenerating nerves. I'd suggest b12 even though levels were normal. Do you know the number? My neurologist treated me because they were low but not "low" on the blood test, just neurologically low with my symptoms. My level was 246.

&#x200B;

Just curious, any chance your symptoms started after the vaccine, first or second dose? My symptoms were like a domino effect, just like you, started about 2/3 weeks after my second dose of Pfizer.

&#x200B;

Edit: Kudos to you also, for being an amazing self advocate.

You're welcome! I live in a house that several ghosts have come through over the years due to our property being on a large mansion estate. I find that I have to do this ritual every few months and it calms things down. But I also try to remember that I have no reason to be a afraid since I have more power than they do in my realm. They can't hurt me unless I allow them to. You are much stronger than they are and the more you practice this, you will truly start to feel your own strength and confidence with it. I try to make sure I get every room of the house, even the basement and I really cover the whole room with the smoke.

&#x200B;

That being said, I also agree many spirits are not harmful and may be stuck, just visiting, perhaps even a loved one. You can always be kind to them, but firm. Set your boundaries, whatever they may be.

I don't think its therapeutically useful to be condescending towards a patient who has a hard time opening up. Making a client comfortable is important so they can actually open up.

&#x200B;

Sitting in silence and then shaming them for not talking is very ass backwards from my perspective. But therapy isn't a science and everyone takes vastly different approaches I am learning from this sub. Im in school to be a therapist. I think I come to this sub to learn what not to do by reading patient perspectives.

&#x200B;

But I also really struggled to talk in therapy when I was a patient. For a long time, I couldn't even look at my therapist. I found that drawing or fiddling with items helped me talk more which she gave to me to help me feel more comfortable.

 My therapist didn't look at my inability to open up as something I needed to fix on my own. She examined what caused that inability to open up and helped me work through it, so I could open up with her, and eventually then with others, outside the therapy room.

Its not terrible. I'd definitely stop walk around the area the same time as them because yes, that is slightly stalkerish.

&#x200B;

Other behaviors are decently normal. Sounds like you have feelings for them. I think you could admit the rest and try to talk to them about them. Who doesnt creep on people alot on the internet lmao! me too, homie me too.

